[2026-07-20T08:24:13.543Z] [INFO]         "text": "# CI/CD Gap Analysis — `link-assistant/formal-ai` vs. link-foundation pipeline templates\n\nScope: `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784535043401/.github/**`, the rust/js/python `*-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template` repos, and `link-assistant/hive-mind/docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md` (380 lines). No repo files were modified.\n\n## 1. Inventory of `.github/` in formal-ai\n\n`.github/` contains **only** `workflows/release.yml` (1625 lines) and `workflows/desktop-release.yml` (650 lines). There are **no** `.github/actions/*` composite actions, **no** `.github/dependabot.yml`, no issue/PR templates, no `CODEOWNERS`.\n\n### `release.yml` — \"CI/CD Pipeline\"\n\nTriggers (L3–L30): `push` → `main`; `pull_request` (opened/synchronize/reopened); `workflow_dispatch` (inputs `release_mode` ∈ {instant, changelog-pr}, `bump_type`, `description`).\nConcurrency L36–L42: `cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.ref != 'refs/heads/main' }}`. `permissions: contents: read` (L33).\n\n| Job | Line | `if:` (condensed) | Runs on PR? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `detect-changes` | 62 | `github.event_name != 'workflow_dispatch'` | yes |\n| `changelog` (fragment check) | 93 | `event == pull_request && any-code-changed` | **PR only** |\n| `version-check` | 117 | `event == pull_request` | **PR only** |\n| `lint` (fmt, clippy, `cargo metadata --locked`, `cargo doc` ×2, file-size, terminology, hardcoded-language) | 143 | `always() && !cancelled() && (push ‖ dispatch ‖ any-code/rs/toml/docs/workflow-changed)` | yes |\n| `test` (matrix, ubuntu only) | 334 | same shape, minus `docs-changed` | yes |\n| `coverage` | 396 | `push ‖ dispatch ‖ rs-changed ‖ toml-changed` | yes (if rs/toml) |\n| `build` (cargo build --release, package, crate-size) | 470 | `needs.lint==success && needs.test==success` | yes |\n| `auto-release` (publish crates.io, Docker GHCR+Hub, tag, GH release) | 508 | `event==push && ref==refs/heads/main && build success` | **no — main push only** |\n| `manual-release` | 761 | `event==workflow_dispatch && release_mode=='instant'` | **no** |\n| `changelog-pr` | 979 | `workflow_dispatch && release_mode=='changelog-pr'` | **no** |\n| `test-e2e-local` | 1031 | `push ‖ dispatch ‖ any-code-changed` | yes |\n| `test-agent-cli-e2e` | 1111 | `push ‖ dispatch ‖ any-code/rs/toml/workflow-changed` | yes |\n| `deploy-pages` | 1431 | `build success && ((push&&main&&auto-release success) ‖ (dispatch&&instant&&manual-release success))` | **no** |\n| `test-e2e-pages` | 1582 | `needs.deploy-pages.result == 'success'` | **no** |\n\n### `desktop-release.yml`\n\nTriggers (L31–L41): `workflow_dispatch(tag)`, `release: [published]`, `workflow_run: workflows:[\"CI/CD Pipeline\"] types:[completed]`. Concurrency L53–54 (`cancel-in-progress: false`).\nJobs: `resolve` (L65, `if:` L81 — `event != workflow_run || (head_branch=='main' && conclusion not in {cancelled,skipped})`), `build` (L113, `needs.resolve.outputs.should_build=='true'`, Tauri desktop matrix), `vscode` (L451, same gate, packages `.vsix`), `finalize` (L532, `always() && should_build`). **None of these ever run on a pull_request.**\n\n## 2. Template file trees\n\n**rust template** — `.github/actions/setup-buildx-resilient/action.yml`, `.github/workflows/release.yml`; `scripts/`: bump-version, check-cargo-lock, check-changelog-fragment, check-crate-size, check-file-size, check-release-needed, check-version-modification, collect-changelog, create-changelog-fragment, create-github-release, detect-code-changes, get-bump-type, get-version, git-config, publish-crate, release-naming, rust-paths, smoke-test-published-crate, version-and-commit, wait-for-crate (all `.rs`).\nJobs: detect-changes(56) · changelog(86) · version-check(110) · **cargo-lock(137)** · lint(167, `needs:[detect-changes,cargo-lock]`) · test(219) · coverage(279) · build(335) · auto-release(373) · manual-release(554) · changelog-pr(712) · deploy-docs(771).\n\n**js template** — `.github/actions/{publish-dockerhub,setup-buildx-resilient}/action.yml`, `.github/workflows/{release,example-app,links}.yml`; 30+ `scripts/*.mjs` incl. `simulate-fresh-merge.sh`, `check-file-line-limits.sh`, `check-web-archive.mjs`, `push-main-with-rebase-retry.sh`.\nJobs: detect-changes(53) · test-compilation(80) · **check-file-line-limits(97)** · version-check(128) · changeset-check(147) · lint(190, incl. **secretlint** L234) · test(240) · **validate-docs(333)** · release(377) · instant-release(482) · docker-publish(552) · changeset-pr(595). `scripts/simulate-fresh-merge.sh` is invoked in three jobs (L114, L210, L284).\n\n**python template** — `.github/workflows/{docs,release}.yml`; `scripts/`: bump_version, check_file_size, create_github_release, create_manual_changeset, detect_code_changes, format_release_notes, publish_to_pypi, release_naming, smoke_test_published_package, validate_changeset, version_and_commit (all `.py`).\n\n## 3. Best-practices checklist → status\n\n| # | Practice (BEST-PRACTICES.md) | formal-ai | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `detect-changes` job gating all others | ✅ | `release.yml:62-91`, `scripts/detect-code-changes.rs` |\n| 2 | File-size limit enforced in CI | ⚠️ present but buried in `lint` | `release.yml:223-225` (`scripts/check-file-size.rs`); templates run it as its own fast job (js `check-file-line-limits`, L97) |\n| 3 | Automated formatting (rustfmt) | ✅ | `release.yml` \"Check formatting\" step in `lint` |\n| 4 | Static analysis (clippy) | ✅ | `lint` job, `RUSTFLAGS: -Dwarnings` (L51) |\n| 5 | Fast-fail job ordering | ⚠️ partial | `build` gates on lint+test (L474-475), but fmt/file-size/clippy/`cargo doc`/e2e-ish checks are all one 10-min `lint` job — no cheap 7-30 s tier |\n| 6 | Changeset/changelog versioning, docs-only exempt | ✅ | `changelog` job L93-98 |\n| 7 | **Validate the actual merge result** (`simulate-fresh-merge`) | ❌ absent | no match for `simulate`/`merge origin` anywhere in `.github/`; cf. js template L114/210/284 |\n| 8 | Pre-commit hooks | ❌ not in `.github`; no hook config found | — |\n| 9 | Release automation, dual trigger, validated | ✅ | `auto-release` L508, `manual-release` L761 |\n| 10 | Concurrency control, `!cancelled()` not `always()` | ⚠️ | group/cancel correct (L36-42) but every job uses `always() && !cancelled()` (L151, 343, 401, 475, 512, 1035, 1115, 1437) — `always()` defeats cancellation propagation; only `test-e2e-pages` (L1585) uses the recommended bare `!cancelled()` |\n| 11 | **Secrets detection** (secretlint/trufflehog) | ❌ absent | no `secretlint`/`trufflehog` match; js template L234 |\n| 12 | Documentation validation (size, links, lychee) | ⚠️ partial | `cargo doc -D warnings` L201-217 validates rustdoc only; no `validate-docs` job, no link checker (js `validate-docs` L333; js `links.yml`) |\n| — | `cargo-lock` guard as separate job | ⚠️ inline | `release.yml` \"Verify Cargo.lock is synchronized\" inside `lint`; rust template has dedicated `cargo-lock` job (L137) that `lint`/`test`/`coverage` depend on |\n| — | `.github/actions/setup-buildx-resilient` composite | ❌ | formal-ai uses raw `docker/setup-buildx-action@v4` (L626, L855) |\n| — | `dependabot.yml` | ❌ absent | `.github/` contains only `workflows/` |\n\n## 4. Checks that CANNOT gate a PR (the core of issue #808)\n\nEverything below runs **only** on push-to-main / release / `workflow_dispatch`, so a PR can merge while any of it is broken:\n\n1. **Docker image build** — `docker/build-push-action@v7` at `release.yml:650`, `:710` (auto-release) and `:877`, `:936` (manual-release). A `Dockerfile` regression is invisible until after merge and after crates.io publish.\n2. **`verify-docker-runtime.sh`** — only reachable from the release jobs.\n3. **crates.io packaging/publish path** — `publish-crate.rs`, `wait-for-crate.rs`, `smoke-test-published-crate.sh`: only in `auto-release`/`manual-release` (L508/L761). (`build` L470 does run `cargo package --list` + crate-size on PRs, so partial coverage exists.)\n4. **`deploy-pages`** (`release.yml:1431`) — Pages artifact assembly, `stamp-pages-artifact.sh`, `cargo doc` for `/docs/api`, `wait-for-pages-deployment.sh`. Never exercised pre-merge.\n5. **`test-e2e-pages`** (`release.yml:1582`) — the entire GitHub-Pages Playwright suite is post-deploy only.\n6. **`desktop-release.yml` `build`** (`desktop-release.yml:113`) — Tauri desktop builds for all OS targets, incl. macOS signing. A change to `src-tauri/**` or the signing steps is only discovered after a release tag exists.\n7. **`desktop-release.yml` `vscode`** (`:451`) — `.vsix` packaging.\n8. **`desktop-release.yml` `finalize`** (`:532`) — SHA256SUMS + provenance.\n9. **`resolve` / `scripts/desktop-release-resolve.sh`** (`:65`) — release-resolution logic changes are untestable in a PR.\n10. **`changelog-pr`** (`release.yml:979`) — dispatch-only.\n11. **Version-bump machinery** — `version-and-commit.rs`, `get-bump-type.rs`, `collect-changelog.rs`, `create-github-release.rs`: executed only inside release jobs. (`version-and-commit-tests.rs` exists in `scripts/` but is not wired into any workflow step — worth confirming it runs under `cargo test`.)\n\nAlso note `coverage` (L401) omits `workflow-changed`, so a workflow-only PR skips it, and `test`/`coverage`/`lint` conditions each list a different subset of `detect-changes` outputs — drift risk.\n\n## 5. Recommended minimal diffs\n\n**(a) PR-gate the Docker build** — add to `release.yml`, before `auto-release`:\n\n```yaml\n  docker-pr-check:\n    name: Docker Build Check\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    timeout-minutes: 20\n    needs: [detect-changes]\n    if: >-\n      !cancelled() && github.event_name == 'pull_request' &&\n      (needs.detect-changes.outputs.any-code-changed == 'true' ||\n       needs.detect-changes.outputs.workflow-changed == 'true')\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v6\n      - run: bash scripts/free-runner-disk.sh\n      - uses: docker/setup-buildx-action@v4\n      - uses: docker/build-push-action@v7\n        with: { context: ., push: false, load: true, tags: formal-ai:pr, cache-from: type=gha, cache-to: type=gha,mode=max }\n      - run: bash scripts/verify-docker-runtime.sh\n```\nRequires `docker-changed` be added to `detect-changes` outputs (`release.yml:67-71`) and to `scripts/detect-code-changes.rs`.\n\n**(b) PR-gate desktop/VS Code builds** — add `pull_request:` to `desktop-release.yml:31` and a dry-run path:\n```yaml\non:\n  pull_request:\n    paths: ['src-tauri/**', 'editors/**', '.github/workflows/desktop-release.yml', 'scripts/desktop-release-resolve.sh']\n```\nplus in `resolve` (L81) `github.event_name == 'pull_request' ||` and in `build`/`vscode` `if: needs.resolve.outputs.should_build == 'true' || github.event_name == 'pull_request'`, with all upload/sign/publish steps guarded by `if: github.event_name != 'pull_request'`. Cheapest variant: restrict the PR matrix to `ubuntu-latest` only.\n\n**(c) PR-gate the Pages artifact** — split `deploy-pages` (L1431) into `build-pages` (artifact assembly + `cargo doc`, runs on PR) and `deploy-pages` (`needs: build-pages`, keeps the current main/dispatch `if:`). Run `test-e2e-local` against the built artifact on PRs.\n\n**(d) Fresh-merge validation** — port `scripts/simulate-fresh-merge.sh` from the js template (or reimplement in bash) and insert after `actions/checkout@v6` in `lint` (L166), `test` (L359) and `changelog` (L100):\n```yaml\n      - name: Simulate fresh merge with base branch (PR only)\n        if: github.event_name == 'pull_request'\n        env: { BASE_REF: '${{ github.base_ref }}' }\n        run: bash scripts/simulate-fresh-merge.sh\n```\nNote this needs `fetch-depth: 0` — already set in `lint`/`changelog`, but `test` (L359) uses a bare `actions/checkout@v6`, so add `with: { fetch-depth: 0 }` there.\n\n**(e) Secrets scan** — one step in `lint`:\n```yaml\n      - name: Secrets scan\n        run: npx --yes -p secretlint -p @secretlint/secretlint-rule-preset-recommend secretlint \"**/*\"\n```\n\n**(f) Fast-fail tier** — extract `check-file-size.rs` + `cargo metadata --locked` from `lint` into two ~20 s jobs (`check-file-line-limits`, `cargo-lock`, mirroring rust template L137) and make `lint`/`test`/`coverage` `needs:` them.\n\n**(g) Cancellation semantics** — replace `always() && !cancelled() &&` with `!cancelled() &&` at L151, L343, L401, L475, L512, L767, L1035, L1115, L1437. The inline comments claim `always()` is needed because `detect-changes` is skipped on `workflow_dispatch`; that is true for `always()` vs. default, but `!cancelled()` alone already evaluates on skipped dependencies (actions/runner#491 applies to the default condition, not to `!cancelled()`), and `always()` is what breaks cancellation propagation.\n\n**(h) Add `.github/dependabot.yml`** (cargo, npm for `tests/e2e`, github-actions ecosystems) — present in neither formal-ai nor the templates, but recommended.\n\n## 6. Defects found in the TEMPLATES (report upstream)\n\n**D1 — `link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template`: no Docker/artifact PR gate.** `release.yml` builds and pushes Docker images only inside `auto-release` (L373) / `manual-release` (L554). Repro: create a PR breaking `Dockerfile`; the full pipeline is green, and the failure surfaces only after merge, *after* `cargo publish` has already run in the same job — leaving a published crate with no matching image. Workaround: the `docker-pr-check` job in §5(a). Fix: upstream should add that job and reuse `.github/actions/setup-buildx-resilient` with `push: false` on PRs.\n\n**D2 — rust template is missing `simulate-fresh-merge`.** The js template ships `scripts/simulate-fresh-merge.sh` and calls it in three jobs (js `release.yml` L114/210/284); the rust template calls it nowhere, and BEST-PRACTICES §7 declares it mandatory. Repro: open PR A and PR B touching the same file; merge A; B's checks still validate the stale merge preview and pass. Workaround: add the step manually. Fix: port the script (it is language-agnostic bash) into the rust and python templates.\n\n**D3 — rust and python templates have no secrets scan.** BEST-PRACTICES §11 requires one; only the js template has `secretlint` (L234). Fix: add the same `npx secretlint` step (or `trufflehog` for non-Node repos) to `lint` in both.\n\n**D4 — python template lacks a `.github/actions/` directory and any Docker publishing path**, so `check-docker-publish`/`publish-dockerhub` equivalents are absent despite being documented as template features.\n\n**D5 — BEST-PRACTICES.md §10 contradicts the templates.** The doc says \"Use `!cancelled()` instead of `always()` so cancellation propagates,\" yet rust template `release.yml` L340 and the js/python equivalents use `always() && !cancelled() && …` throughout — which every downstream repo (including formal-ai, L151 etc.) has copied verbatim along with a comment asserting `always()` is required. Fix: either correct the templates to `!cancelled()` or amend the doc to explain the `workflow_dispatch`/skipped-dependency caveat; today the two disagree and downstream repos inherit the weaker semantics."
