[2026-07-20T08:33:31.518Z] [INFO]         "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\n   The user gave a single task brief: solve GitHub issue https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/808 on the prepared branch `issue-808-bf5af32dbcdd` in `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784535043401`, updating the existing PR https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/809. Explicit instructions, verbatim in intent:\n   - \"Download all logs and collect data related about the issue to this repository, and compile that data into the ./dev/log/issues/808/pulls/809 folder.\"\n   - \"Use the collected evidence to do a deep analysis (search online for additional facts and data), reconstruct the timeline/sequence of events, list each and every requirement from the issue, find the root cause of each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement. Also check online for known existing components/libraries that solve a similar problem or can help.\"\n   - \"If there is not enough data to find the actual root cause, add debug output and a verbose mode (if not already present) so the root cause can be found on the next iteration. Keep the default state switched off.\"\n   - \"If the issue is related to another repository/project, report issues on GitHub for that project when possible. Each report must contain reproducible examples, workarounds, and suggestions for fixing the issue in code.\"\n   - \"Double-check that the requirements are fully applied to the entire codebase: if an issue exists in multiple places, apply it in all of them.\"\n\n   Issue #808 itself requires: fix all false positives, false negatives, warnings and errors in CI/CD; compare all workflow/CI files against three templates (`link-foundation/rust-`, `js-`, `python-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template`) and reuse their best practices, reporting the same issue upstream to templates if found there; follow `link-assistant/hive-mind/docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md`; \"plan and execute everything in this single pull request... until it is each and every requirement fully addressed.\"\n\n   Issue comment 5020083365 (a repo member, not the current user turn) adds: \"All checks must be in Pull Request stage, not only on main, so each pull request has a chance to produce actually working release. Fix it here. All requirements of all checks must be done/addressed in this pull request.\"\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GitHub Actions workflows: `release.yml` (\"CI/CD Pipeline\", 15 jobs) and `desktop-release.yml` (\"Desktop Release\", 4 jobs: resolve/build/vscode/finalize), `workflow_run` chaining, `detect-changes` gating, concurrency groups, `always() && !cancelled()` vs `!cancelled()`.\n   - Electron packaging: `electron-builder` 26.15.3, `app-builder-lib`, `@electron/osx-sign`, custom `mac.sign` hook, `mac.signIgnore`, ad-hoc codesign (`--sign -`), hardened runtime, entitlements, `extraResources`, Chrome for Testing / Playwright browser runtime bundling.\n   - macOS codesign semantics: \"unsealed contents present in the root directory of an embedded framework\" (non-versioned framework layout cannot be re-signed).\n   - Rust `rust-script` CLI scripts in `scripts/` (self-hosting-metric.rs, version-and-commit.rs, check-*.rs).\n   - Self-hosting metric invariant: `Formal-AI-Session` + `Formal-AI-Evidence` git trailers; evidence file must contain \"formal-ai\" and the exact session id (CONTRIBUTING.md lines 94–106).\n   - Node `node --test`, `process.stdout` vs `process.stderr` buffering semantics on POSIX pipes.\n   - `changelog.d/` fragment convention with `bump:` frontmatter.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - `dev/log/issues/808/pulls/809/analysis.md` (CREATED, ~250 lines)\n     - The main deliverable: evidence index, timeline, requirements R1–R6, root cause of Failure A and B, PR-gate backlog (8 items), template gap table, upstream defects T1–T5, reusable-components section, and list of changes. Also serves as the `Formal-AI-Evidence` file (contains \"formal-ai\" and session id `issue-808-claude-20260720`).\n\n   - `dev/log/issues/808/pulls/809/ci-logs/` (CREATED)\n     - `README.md` documenting each excerpt, how to re-download full logs (`gh run view <id> --repo link-assistant/formal-ai --log`), and the three decisive facts (1506 browser-runtime paths signed individually; zero `[adhoc-sign-mac]` lines despite debug=1; zero `Skipped...` lines).\n     - `run-29723467001-auto-release.log` (27 lines), `run-29719602956-excerpt.log` (6), `run-29724500254-macos-codesign-excerpt.log` (39), `run-29720321919-macos-codesign-excerpt.log` (39). The 2.5–3.5 MB raw logs and `.json` metadata were deleted after extraction.\n\n   - `desktop/package.json` (MODIFIED) — the primary fix for Failure A; makes the exclusion independent of the custom sign hook:\n     ```json\n     \"hardenedRuntime\": true,\n     \"signIgnore\": [\n       \"/Contents/Resources/browser-runtime/\"\n     ],\n     ```\n\n   - `desktop/scripts/adhoc-sign-mac.cjs` (MODIFIED) — diagnostics to stderr + unconditional entry banner:\n     ```js\n     // Diagnostics go to stderr, never stdout. electron-builder's own logger and\n     // electron-osx-sign's `debug` output both use stderr; interleaving there keeps\n     // the sign trace readable in GitHub Actions logs, and stderr is the stream that\n     // survives when electron-builder aborts the CLI on a signing error.\n     function log(message) {\n       process.stderr.write(`[adhoc-sign-mac] ${message}\\n`);\n     }\n\n     function debugLog(message) {\n       if (isDebugEnabled()) {\n         log(message);\n       }\n     }\n     ```\n     and inside `module.exports = async function adhocSignMac(signOptions)`:\n     ```js\n       // One unconditional line. Run 29724500254 failed inside electron-osx-sign\n       // while FORMAL_AI_MACOS_SIGN_DEBUG=1 was set, yet the log contained no\n       // `[adhoc-sign-mac]` output at all, so we could not tell whether this hook\n       // ever ran. This banner settles that question on every future run; the\n       // per-file trace stays behind the env var and off by default.\n       log(`hook entered (debug=${isDebugEnabled() ? 'on' : 'off'})`);\n\n       const upstreamOptionsForFile = signOptions.optionsForFile;\n     ```\n     (Existing `isDebugEnabled()` reads `process.env.FORMAL_AI_MACOS_SIGN_DEBUG === '1'` — default off, unchanged.)\n\n   - `desktop/scripts/adhoc-sign-mac.test.cjs` (MODIFIED, appended third test):\n     ```js\n     test('electron-builder config excludes the bundled browser runtime from signing', () => {\n       const { signIgnore } = require('../package.json').build.mac;\n       assert.ok(Array.isArray(signIgnore) && signIgnore.length > 0, 'mac.signIgnore must be configured');\n       const matches = (filePath) => signIgnore.some((pattern) => new RegExp(pattern).test(filePath));\n       const app = '/Users/runner/work/formal-ai/formal-ai/desktop/release/mac/formal-ai Desktop.app';\n       assert.equal(matches(`${app}/Contents/Resources/browser-runtime/Frameworks/Google Chrome for Testing Framework.framework`), true);\n       assert.equal(matches(`${app}/Contents/Resources/browser-runtime/chrome`), true);\n       assert.equal(matches(`${app}/Contents/MacOS/formal-ai Desktop`), false);\n       assert.equal(matches(app), false);\n     });\n     ```\n     Result: `# tests 3 / # pass 3 / # fail 0`.\n\n   - `.github/workflows/release.yml` (MODIFIED) — new PR-stage job inserted before `version-check`:\n     ```yaml\n       evidence-check:\n         name: Self-Hosting Evidence Check\n         runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n         timeout-minutes: 10\n         if: github.event_name == 'pull_request'\n         steps:\n           - uses: actions/checkout@v6\n             with:\n               fetch-depth: 0\n           - name: Setup Rust\n             uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable\n           - name: Install rust-script\n             run: bash scripts/install-rust-script.sh\n           - name: Validate Formal-AI trailers on this pull request\n             env:\n               GITHUB_BASE_REF: ${{ github.base_ref }}\n             run: |\n               set -euo pipefail\n               base=\"origin/${GITHUB_BASE_REF}\"\n               merge_base=\"$(git merge-base \"$base\" HEAD)\"\n               echo \"Validating commits in ${merge_base}..HEAD\"\n               rust-script scripts/self-hosting-metric.rs --since \"$merge_base\" --until HEAD\n     ```\n     (preceded by a comment block explaining run 29723467001 and why the gate moved to PR stage)\n\n   - `.gitignore` (MODIFIED) — lines 59–62 ignore `*.log`, `logs/`, `ci-logs/`; added after the existing `!docs/case-studies/**/*.log`:\n     ```\n     # Development-log CI evidence, committed alongside the analysis that cites it\n     # (see dev/log/issues/*/pulls/*/ci-logs/README.md).\n     !dev/log/**/ci-logs/\n     !dev/log/**/ci-logs/*.log\n     ```\n\n   - `changelog.d/20260720_140000_issue_808_ci_cd_fixes.md` (CREATED) — `bump: patch`, Fixed (signIgnore, stderr diagnostics) and Added (PR evidence job) entries.\n\n   - `experiments/stdout-loss.cjs` (CREATED) — records a REJECTED hypothesis with its negative result.\n\n   - Read-only but important:\n     - `scripts/self-hosting-metric.rs` — `commit_has_formal_ai_evidence` (lines 111–147) raises `no committed {EVIDENCE_TRAILER} in {commit} records session {session}`; `measure(repo, since, until)`; CLI accepts `--since/--until/--repo/--ledger/--record-release/--trailing-window`.\n     - `scripts/version-and-commit.rs:635-641` — calls `record_self_hosting_release`, `exit(1)` on error (the release-time gate).\n     - `desktop/build/entitlements.mac.plist` — already grants `com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation` (proving the electron-builder warning is a false positive).\n     - `app-builder-lib/out/mac/MacTargetHelper.js:52-112` and `out/options/macOptions.d.ts:163` — proof `signIgnore` works independently of the custom sign hook.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n\n   - **Failure A — macOS ad-hoc codesign fails** (`unsealed contents present in the root directory of an embedded framework` on `Google Chrome for Testing Framework.framework`), runs 29720321919 and 29724500254. Root cause: the exclusion lived only in the custom `mac.sign` hook and was provably not in effect (1506 browser-runtime paths individually signed, zero `Skipped...` lines, zero `[adhoc-sign-mac]` lines despite `FORMAL_AI_MACOS_SIGN_DEBUG=1`). Fixed by declaring `build.mac.signIgnore` in `desktop/package.json` (applied by `MacTargetHelper.buildSignOptions()` regardless of the hook) plus stderr diagnostics + unconditional entry banner to settle hook-execution on the next run.\n   - **Failure B — Auto Release aborts** (`no committed Formal-AI-Evidence in 10e65ae2… records session issue-804-claude-20260720`), runs 29719602956 and 29723467001. Root cause: commit `10e65ae2`'s evidence file `dev/log/issues/804/pulls/805/analysis.md` contains neither \"formal-ai\" nor the session id; the invariant was enforced only at release time on main, after merge. Reproduced exactly locally. Fixed with the PR-stage `evidence-check` job reusing the same script (no duplicated logic).\n   - **My own hypothesis error**: I hypothesized the missing `[adhoc-sign-mac]` lines were caused by async stdout buffering discarded on `process.exit()`. I wrote `experiments/stdout-loss.cjs` and it did NOT reproduce (200/200 lines survived on Linux, since Node writes synchronously to POSIX pipes). I recorded the rejection in the script header and in analysis.md rather than shipping a wrong explanation.\n   - **ci-logs were untracked**: `git check-ignore` showed `.gitignore:62: ci-logs/`. Fixed by adding `dev/log/**/ci-logs/` negations, following the existing `!docs/case-studies/**/*.log` precedent.\n   - **Logs too large to commit** (2.7 MB + 2.5 MB + 3.5 MB): replaced with filtered excerpts (39/27/6 lines) plus a README explaining the filter and how to re-download.\n   - **`python3 -c \"import yaml\"` failed** (ModuleNotFoundError). Worked around by validating with `js-yaml` from `desktop/node_modules`.\n   - **Subagent inaccuracy**: the background research agent described `desktop-release.yml`'s build job as \"Tauri desktop matrix\"; it is actually an Electron/electron-builder matrix. I used my own verified reading for all details I acted on.\n\n   No corrective user feedback was received during the session.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n\n   Solved: both red default-branch failures root-caused with committed evidence, fixed, and covered by a regression test (signIgnore) and a new PR gate (evidence). Timeline reconstructed (05:38→08:10 UTC 2026-07-20), including establishing that the five `skipped` Desktop Release runs are correct downstream behaviour of the `workflow_run` gate, not a defect. Established the electron-builder disable-library-validation warning is a false positive (entitlement already present).\n\n   Ongoing/unresolved: the precise reason the custom sign hook produced no output at all in CI is still unexplained; the unconditional banner was added specifically so the next run answers it. Requirement R2 (all checks at PR stage) is only partially addressed — one of nine identified gaps is fixed.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The single user message was the task brief: \"Download all logs and collect data related about the issue to this repository, and compile that data into the ./dev/log/issues/808/pulls/809 folder. Use the collected evidence to do a deep analysis (search online for additional facts and data), reconstruct the timeline/sequence of events, list each and every requirement from the issue, find the root cause of each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement. Also check online for known existing components/libraries that solve a similar problem or can help. If there is not enough data to find the actual root cause, add debug output and a verbose mode (if not already present) so the root cause can be found on the next iteration. Keep the default state switched off. If the issue is related to another repository/project, report issues on GitHub for that project when possible. Each report must contain reproducible examples, workarounds, and suggestions for fixing the issue in code. Double-check that the requirements are fully applied to the entire codebase: if an issue exists in multiple places, apply it in all of them. Proceed.\" — preceded by the issue/branch/working-dir/PR context lines.\n   - A final instruction to produce this summary as text only, with no tool calls.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **R2 (main remaining work): make checks gate pull requests.** Nine identified gaps, ranked, from analysis.md §6:\n     1. `desktop-release.yml` `build` (the currently-red job) — add `pull_request:` trigger with build-only path, guarding all upload/attest/publish steps with `if: github.event_name != 'pull_request'`. **This was in progress.**\n     2. `desktop-release.yml` `vscode` (.vsix packaging) and `finalize` (SHA256SUMS + provenance).\n     3. Docker image build + `scripts/verify-docker-runtime.sh` (currently only in `auto-release`/`manual-release`).\n     4. `deploy-pages` artifact assembly / `test-e2e-pages`.\n     5. `scripts/desktop-release-resolve.sh` logic; version-bump machinery.\n   - **R3/R5 template + best-practices gaps**: add `simulate-fresh-merge.sh`, secrets scan (secretlint/trufflehog), dedicated fast `cargo-lock` and file-size jobs, doc/link validation, `.github/actions/setup-buildx-resilient` composite, `.github/dependabot.yml`, replace `always() && !cancelled()` with `!cancelled()` at release.yml lines 151, 343, 401, 475, 512, 767, 1035, 1115, 1437.\n   - **R4 upstream issue reports** (documented in analysis.md §8, not yet filed): T1 no Docker PR gate in rust template; T2 `simulate-fresh-merge` missing from rust/python templates; T3 no secrets scan in rust/python templates; T4 CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md §10 contradicts all three templates on `!cancelled()`; T5 electron-builder false-positive disable-library-validation warning.\n   - Update PR #809 title/description (`gh pr edit`), merge main into the branch, verify CI, and `gh pr ready 809`.\n\n8. Current Work:\n\n   Immediately before the summary request, one commit was already made and pushed to `issue-808-bf5af32dbcdd`:\n\n   ```\n   fix(ci): stop macOS ad-hoc signing on bundled browser runtime and gate evidence trailers in PRs\n   ...\n   Formal-AI-Session: issue-808-claude-20260720\n   Formal-AI-Evidence: dev/log/issues/808/pulls/809/analysis.md\n   ```\n   verified with `rust-script scripts/self-hosting-metric.rs --since main --until HEAD` → `99.44% (536/539 changed lines; 1/2 commits)`, exit 0, then `git push -q origin issue-808-bf5af32dbcdd`.\n\n   I then stated: \"Now the highest-value R2 gap: desktop packaging never runs on PRs — the very job that is red.\" and was reading `.github/workflows/desktop-release.yml` — lines 28–120 (triggers `workflow_dispatch`/`release`/`workflow_run`; `permissions: contents: read`; concurrency `desktop-release-${{ ... }}` with `cancel-in-progress: false`; `resolve` job `if:` on `workflow_run` head_branch/conclusion; outputs `tag`, `should_build` from `scripts/desktop-release-resolve.sh`), lines 113–205 (the `build` job: `needs: resolve`, `if: needs.resolve.outputs.should_build == 'true'`, six-target matrix ubuntu-latest/ubuntu-24.04-arm/macos-15-intel/macos-14/windows-latest/windows-11-arm, `permissions: contents: write, id-token: write, attestations: write`, checkout `ref: ${{ needs.resolve.outputs.tag }}`, cargo build, node setup, `prepare-resources.mjs`, `mac_secrets` detection, and the three `Package desktop app` steps), and lines 250–460 (macOS DMG smoke test, Linux/Windows artifact smoke test, `Collect artifacts and checksums`, `Attest build provenance` via `actions/attest@v4`, `Upload assets to release` via `gh release upload`, `Upload checksum fragment`, and the start of the `vscode` job).\n\n   No edits to `desktop-release.yml` had been made yet.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n\n   Edit `.github/workflows/desktop-release.yml` to run the desktop build on pull requests in build-only mode, per the plan recorded in analysis.md §6 item 5 (\"Item 5 is the highest-value gap: had `desktop-release.yml`'s macOS build run on pull requests, Failure A would have been caught in the PR that introduced the bundled browser runtime instead of in a release.\") and my last statement: \"Now the highest-value R2 gap: desktop packaging never runs on PRs — the very job that is red.\"\n\n   Concretely: add a `pull_request:` trigger (paths-filtered to `desktop/**`, `.github/workflows/desktop-release.yml`, `scripts/desktop-release-resolve.sh`); relax `resolve`'s `if:` and `build`/`vscode`'s `if: needs.resolve.outputs.should_build == 'true'` to also admit `github.event_name == 'pull_request'`; make the PR path skip `ref: ${{ needs.resolve.outputs.tag }}` (build the PR head) and guard `Attest build provenance`, `Upload assets to release`, and `finalize` with `if: github.event_name != 'pull_request'`, keeping the smoke tests active. Then validate the YAML with the `js-yaml` one-liner, commit with the Formal-AI trailers, push, and update PR #809's title/description.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/box/.claude/projects/-tmp-gh-issue-solver-1784535043401/a7583710-f266-4c39-b5cf-8583e137ffd4.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."
