[2026-07-20T08:35:33.800Z] [INFO]         "content": "186\t## 6. Checks that still cannot gate a pull request (R2 backlog)\n187\t\n188\tDerived from a full reading of both workflows. Each item runs only on\n189\tpush-to-`main`, `release`, `workflow_run` or `workflow_dispatch`:\n190\t\n191\t1. Docker image build + `scripts/verify-docker-runtime.sh` (`release.yml`\n192\t   `auto-release` / `manual-release` only).\n193\t2. crates.io publish path (`publish-crate.rs`, `wait-for-crate.rs`,\n194\t   `smoke-test-published-crate.sh`). Partially covered on PRs by `build`'s\n195\t   `cargo package --list` + crate-size check.\n196\t3. `deploy-pages` — Pages artifact assembly, `stamp-pages-artifact.sh`,\n197\t   `cargo doc` for `/docs/api`.\n198\t4. `test-e2e-pages` — the whole GitHub-Pages Playwright suite is post-deploy.\n199\t5. `desktop-release.yml` `build` — **the very job that is red today**. Desktop\n200\t   packaging and macOS signing are only exercised after a release exists.\n201\t6. `desktop-release.yml` `vscode` (`.vsix` packaging) and `finalize`\n202\t   (SHA256SUMS + provenance).\n203\t7. `scripts/desktop-release-resolve.sh` release-resolution logic.\n204\t8. Version-bump machinery (`version-and-commit.rs`, `get-bump-type.rs`,\n205\t   `collect-changelog.rs`, `create-github-release.rs`).\n206\t\n207\tItem 5 is the highest-value gap: had `desktop-release.yml`'s macOS build run on\n208\tpull requests, Failure A would have been caught in the PR that introduced the\n209\tbundled browser runtime instead of in a release.\n210\t\n211\t## 7. Gaps versus the templates and CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md\n212\t\n213\tCompared against `link-foundation/{rust,js,python}-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template`\n214\tand `link-assistant/hive-mind/docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md`:\n215\t"
