[2026-07-20T08:42:45.119Z] [INFO]   "description": "cat > /tmp/tpl/eb-issue.md <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n\nWhen ad-hoc signing (`identity: \"-\"` / no signing identity available) with `hardenedRuntime` enabled, electron-builder always logs:\n\n```\n• ad-hoc signing with hardenedRuntime enabled requires the com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation entitlement\n  to prevent app launch failures due to library validation. See https://electron.build/code-signing for details.\n```\n\nIt logs this **even when the configured entitlements file already grants that entitlement**. The check never reads the entitlements, so for correctly-configured projects the warning is a pure false positive — and one that trains people to ignore a warning that is genuinely useful when it applies.\n\nVersion: `app-builder-lib@26.15.3` (via `electron-builder@26.15.3`).\n\n## Where\n\n`src/mac/MacTargetHelper.ts` — in the compiled output, `out/mac/MacTargetHelper.js:36-41`:\n\n```js\nif (qualifier === \"-\") {\n    if (MacTargetHelper.isHardenedRuntimeEnabledForSigning(isMas, config)) {\n        log.warn(null, \"ad-hoc signing with hardenedRuntime enabled requires the com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation entitlement \" +\n            \"to prevent app launch failures due to library validation. See https://electron.build/code-signing for details.\");\n    }\n    ...\n```\n\nand\n\n```js\nstatic isHardenedRuntimeEnabledForSigning(isMas, config) {\n    return isMas ? config.hardenedRuntime === true : config.hardenedRuntime !== false;\n}\n```\n\nThe condition is `ad-hoc && hardenedRuntime`. `config.entitlements` is not consulted anywhere in this path.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nMinimal `package.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"build\": {\n    \"appId\": \"com.example.app\",\n    \"mac\": {\n      \"identity\": null,\n      \"hardenedRuntime\": true,\n      \"entitlements\": \"build/entitlements.mac.plist\",\n      \"entitlementsInherit\": \"build/entitlements.mac.plist\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n`build/entitlements.mac.plist` — note the entitlement the warning asks for is present:\n\n```xml\n<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC \"-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN\" \"http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd\">\n<plist version=\"1.0\">\n  <dict>\n    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key><true/>\n    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key><true/>\n    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key><true/>\n  </dict>\n</plist>\n```\n\n```console\n$ npx electron-builder --mac\n...\n  • ad-hoc signing with hardenedRuntime enabled requires the com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation entitlement …\n```\n\nExpected: no warning, because the entitlement is granted. Actual: warning on every build.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nParse the resolved entitlements plist and warn only if the key is absent or false. Sketch, keeping the current behaviour when the file cannot be read (warn — that is the safe default):\n\n```ts\nprivate static async isLibraryValidationDisabled(config: MacConfiguration, packager: MacPackager): Promise<boolean> {\n  const file = config.entitlements\n  if (file == null) {\n    return false // the default entitlements electron-builder ships do not grant it\n  }\n  try {\n    const parsed = parsePlist(await fs.readFile(await packager.getResource(file), \"utf8\"))\n    return parsed[\"com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation\"] === true\n  } catch (e) {\n    log.debug({ file, error: e.message }, \"cannot read entitlements to validate the ad-hoc hardened-runtime warning\")\n    return false\n  }\n}\n```\n\nthen:\n\n```ts\nif (MacTargetHelper.isHardenedRuntimeEnabledForSigning(isMas, config) &&\n    !(await MacTargetHelper.isLibraryValidationDisabled(config, this.packager))) {\n  log.warn(null, \"ad-hoc signing with hardenedRuntime enabled requires …\")\n}\n```\n\n`plist` is already a dependency of `app-builder-lib`, so no new one is needed. A cheaper variant, if reading the plist here is undesirable, is to demote the message to `log.info` when `config.entitlements` is set explicitly, on the grounds that the user has taken over entitlements management.\n\n## Workaround\n\nNone that suppresses just this line — electron-builder has no per-warning filter. Downstream we document it as a known false positive next to the entitlements file so it is not mistaken for a real signing problem.\n\nFound while debugging macOS ad-hoc signing in `link-assistant/formal-ai` (issue [#808](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/808)). Happy to send the pull request if the approach looks right.\nEOF\ngh issue create --repo electron-userland/electron-builder --title \"False-positive warning: ad-hoc + hardenedRuntime warns about com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation even when the entitlement is granted\" --body-file /tmp/tpl/eb-issue.md",
