[2026-07-20T09:12:19.128Z] [INFO]         "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\n   The single user task brief (from the prior session, still governing): solve GitHub issue https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/808 on branch `issue-808-bf5af32dbcdd` in `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784535043401`, updating existing PR https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/809. Verbatim requirements:\n   - \"Download all logs and collect data related about the issue to this repository, and compile that data into the ./dev/log/issues/808/pulls/809 folder.\"\n   - \"Use the collected evidence to do a deep analysis (search online for additional facts and data), reconstruct the timeline/sequence of events, list each and every requirement from the issue, find the root cause of each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement. Also check online for known existing components/libraries that solve a similar problem or can help.\"\n   - \"If there is not enough data to find the actual root cause, add debug output and a verbose mode (if not already present) so the root cause can be found on the next iteration. Keep the default state switched off.\"\n   - \"If the issue is related to another repository/project, report issues on GitHub for that project when possible. Each report must contain reproducible examples, workarounds, and suggestions for fixing the issue in code.\"\n   - \"Double-check that the requirements are fully applied to the entire codebase: if an issue exists in multiple places, apply it in all of them. Proceed.\"\n\n   Issue #808 itself: fix all false positives, false negatives, warnings and errors in CI/CD; compare all workflow/CI files against `link-foundation/{rust,js,python}-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template` and reuse their best practices, reporting the same defects upstream; follow `link-assistant/hive-mind/docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md`; do everything in this single PR.\n\n   Issue comment 5020083365: \"All checks must be in Pull Request stage, not only on main, so each pull request has a chance to produce actually working release. Fix it here. All requirements of all checks must be done/addressed in this pull request.\"\n\n   Requirement labels used throughout: R1 fix all CI defects; R2 all checks at PR stage; R3 template comparison/adoption; R4 upstream reports; R5 CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md; R6 evidence collection.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GitHub Actions: `pull_request`/`workflow_run`/`release` triggers, path filters, `needs` + skipped-dependency semantics, `!cancelled()` vs `always() && !cancelled()`, concurrency groups, `cancel-in-progress`, matrix builds, `${{ }}` expression escaping, and the YAML pitfall that a bare leading `!` in an inline `if:` is a tag indicator.\n   - electron-builder / `app-builder-lib@26.15.3`: `mac.signIgnore`, `MacTargetHelper.buildSignOptions()`, `isHardenedRuntimeEnabledForSigning()`, ad-hoc signing (`qualifier === \"-\"`), hardened runtime, entitlements plists.\n   - macOS codesign: \"unsealed contents present in the root directory of an embedded framework\" on non-versioned framework layouts (Chrome for Testing).\n   - Docker: buildx `push:false, load:true` for fork-PR-safe builds, `type=gha` layer cache, DinD image + `--privileged`, `verify-formal-ai-dind` runtime contract.\n   - secretlint with `@secretlint/secretlint-rule-preset-recommend`, `.secretlintrc.json`.\n   - Self-hosting metric invariant: `Formal-AI-Session` + `Formal-AI-Evidence` git trailers, validated by `scripts/self-hosting-metric.rs`.\n   - `changelog.d/` fragments with `bump:` frontmatter.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   COMMITTED AND PUSHED THIS SESSION:\n\n   - `.github/workflows/desktop-release.yml` (MODIFIED) — the R2 headline fix:\n     ```yaml\n       # Issue #808: packaging and macOS signing used to run only after a release\n       # existed, so a desktop regression was always discovered post-merge -- which is\n       # exactly how the \"unsealed contents present in the root directory of an\n       # embedded framework\" codesign failure reached main. On pull requests the same\n       # build matrix runs in dry-run mode: everything up to and including the smoke\n       # tests, with every publishing step (attest, release upload, SHA256SUMS)\n       # skipped. Path-filtered so unrelated pull requests do not pay for six runners.\n       pull_request:\n         types: [opened, synchronize, reopened]\n         paths:\n           - 'desktop/**'\n           - 'vscode/**'\n           - '.github/workflows/desktop-release.yml'\n           - 'scripts/desktop-release-resolve.sh'\n           - 'scripts/install-node-dependencies.sh'\n     ```\n     concurrency:\n     ```yaml\n       group: desktop-release-${{ github.event.pull_request.number || github.event.release.tag_name || github.event.inputs.tag || github.event.workflow_run.head_sha || github.run_id }}\n       cancel-in-progress: ${{ github.event_name == 'pull_request' }}\n     ```\n     `resolve` gate (note the extra parenthesis added to close the original clause):\n     ```yaml\n         if: >-\n           github.event_name != 'pull_request' &&\n           (github.event_name != 'workflow_run' ||\n           (github.event.workflow_run.head_branch == 'main' &&\n            github.event.workflow_run.conclusion != 'cancelled' &&\n            github.event.workflow_run.conclusion != 'skipped'))\n     ```\n     `build` and `vscode` gates:\n     ```yaml\n         if: ${{ !cancelled() && (github.event_name == 'pull_request' || needs.resolve.outputs.should_build == 'true') }}\n     ```\n     both checkouts:\n     ```yaml\n             # On pull requests there is no resolved tag: build the PR head, which\n             # is the whole point of the dry run.\n             ref: ${{ github.event_name != 'pull_request' && needs.resolve.outputs.tag || '' }}\n     ```\n     `if: github.event_name != 'pull_request'` added to `Attest build provenance` (both jobs), `Upload assets to release`, `Upload .vsix to release`; `finalize` gate became `if: ${{ always() && github.event_name != 'pull_request' && needs.resolve.outputs.should_build == 'true' }}`.\n\n   - `.github/workflows/release.yml` (MODIFIED, committed) — new `docker-build` job inserted before `version-check`:\n     ```yaml\n       docker-build:\n         name: Docker Image Build & Runtime Check\n         runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n         timeout-minutes: 60\n         needs: [detect-changes]\n         if: github.event_name == 'pull_request' && needs.detect-changes.outputs.any-code-changed == 'true'\n         steps:\n           - uses: actions/checkout@v6\n           - name: Free up runner disk space\n             run: bash scripts/free-runner-disk.sh\n           - name: Set up Docker Buildx\n             uses: docker/setup-buildx-action@v4   # later rewired to ./.github/actions/setup-buildx-resilient\n           - name: Build image\n             uses: docker/build-push-action@v7\n             with:\n               context: .\n               push: false\n               load: true\n               tags: formal-ai:pr-check\n               cache-from: type=gha\n               cache-to: type=gha,mode=max\n           - name: Verify image runtime contract\n             run: |\n               set -euo pipefail\n               docker run --rm --privileged formal-ai:pr-check verify-formal-ai-dind\n     ```\n     Plus all 9 `always() && !cancelled()` → `!cancelled()`, with line 560 rewritten as\n     `    if: ${{ !cancelled() && needs.lint.result == 'success' && needs.test.result == 'success' }}`.\n\n   - `dev/log/issues/808/pulls/809/analysis.md` (MODIFIED, committed) — §1 evidence table rewritten to the excerpt filenames; §6 items 5/6 struck through as fixed with a bullet list of the dry-run design; §8 replaced with a filed-upstream table plus two explicit self-corrections (js template has 0 occurrences of the bad guard; the electron-builder warning is triggered by `qualifier === \"-\" && hardenedRuntime`, not by the custom sign hook); §10 changes list extended to 7 items.\n\n   - `changelog.d/20260720_140000_issue_808_ci_cd_fixes.md` (MODIFIED, committed) — added Fixed entry for the `!cancelled()` guards and Added entries for the desktop/vsix PR packaging and the Docker PR job.\n\n   UNCOMMITTED WORK IN PROGRESS (on disk now):\n\n   - `scripts/simulate-fresh-merge.sh` (NEW, copied verbatim from the js template, `chmod +x`), header adapted:\n     ```bash\n     # Adopted verbatim from link-foundation/js-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template\n     # (issue #808 / R3). GitHub checks out `refs/pull/N/merge`, a merge preview\n     # computed when the PR was last synced -- it does NOT include commits pushed to\n     # the base branch afterwards. A PR can therefore be green against a base that no\n     # longer exists and break `main` on merge.\n     ```\n\n   - `.github/workflows/release.yml` — `lint` job gained (after `checkout` with `fetch-depth: 0`):\n     ```yaml\n           - name: Simulate fresh merge with base branch (PR only)\n             if: github.event_name == 'pull_request'\n             env:\n               BASE_REF: ${{ github.base_ref }}\n             run: bash scripts/simulate-fresh-merge.sh\n     ```\n     `test` job checkout changed to `fetch-depth: 0` with the same step added. New `secrets-scan` job (before `version-check`):\n     ```yaml\n       secrets-scan:\n         name: Secrets Scan\n         runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n         timeout-minutes: 10\n         needs: [detect-changes]\n         if: |\n           !cancelled() && (\n             github.event_name == 'push' ||\n             github.event_name == 'workflow_dispatch' ||\n             needs.detect-changes.outputs.any-code-changed == 'true' ||\n             needs.detect-changes.outputs.docs-changed == 'true' ||\n             needs.detect-changes.outputs.workflow-changed == 'true'\n           )\n         steps:\n           - uses: actions/checkout@v6\n             with:\n               # check-secrets.sh diffs against the base branch / previous commit.\n               fetch-depth: 0\n           - name: Setup Node\n             uses: actions/setup-node@v6\n             with:\n               node-version: 22\n           - name: Check for secrets\n             env:\n               # pull_request -> base branch; push -> the pre-push SHA;\n               # workflow_dispatch has neither, so scan the tip commit.\n               BASE_REF: ${{ github.base_ref || github.event.before || 'HEAD~1' }}\n             run: bash scripts/check-secrets.sh\n     ```\n     All 3 `docker/setup-buildx-action@v4` usages (lines ~177, 766, 995) rewired to `uses: ./.github/actions/setup-buildx-resilient` (the `if:` conditions on the release-job instances were preserved).\n\n   - `scripts/check-secrets.sh` (NEW, `chmod +x`) — diff-scoped secretlint runner with `--all` / explicit-files / `BASE_REF` modes, `FORMAL_AI_SECRETS_DEBUG=1` verbose mode (default off), exclusion of `docs/case-studies/**/*.log` and `dev/log/**/ci-logs/*.log`, and a `HEAD~1` fallback when the base ref does not resolve. Core:\n     ```bash\n     elif [ -n \"${BASE_REF:-}\" ]; then\n       base=\"origin/${BASE_REF}\"\n       git rev-parse --verify --quiet \"$base\" >/dev/null || base=\"${BASE_REF}\"\n       if ! git rev-parse --verify --quiet \"${base}^{commit}\" >/dev/null; then\n         echo \"Base ref '${BASE_REF}' does not resolve here; falling back to HEAD~1\"\n         base=\"HEAD~1\"\n       fi\n       merge_base=\"$(git merge-base \"$base\" HEAD)\"\n       mapfile -d '' files < <(git diff --name-only --diff-filter=ACMRT -z \"$merge_base\" HEAD | exclude)\n     ```\n\n   - `.secretlintrc.json` (NEW, copied from js template):\n     ```json\n     { \"rules\": [ { \"id\": \"@secretlint/secretlint-rule-preset-recommend\" } ] }\n     ```\n\n   - `.secretlintignore` (NEW, created during the abandoned full-tree approach; may now be redundant since `check-secrets.sh` does its own exclusion — needs a keep-or-delete decision).\n\n   - `.github/actions/setup-buildx-resilient/action.yml` (NEW, copied verbatim from the rust template; description block re-attributed to \"Adopted verbatim from link-foundation/rust-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template (issue #808 / R3)\"). Pre-pulls `moby/buildkit:buildx-stable-1` with retries + `mirror.gcr.io` fallback before booting buildx.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **`if: !cancelled() && …` broke YAML** — `unknown tag !<!cancelled()>` at release.yml:560. A bare leading `!` is a YAML tag indicator. Fixed by wrapping that one inline condition in `${{ }}`; block-scalar (`if: |`) forms were unaffected. Verified with `js-yaml` and by grepping that no `if: !` remains.\n   - **Nonexistent `editors/` path filter** — I initially path-filtered `desktop-release.yml` on `editors/**`; `ls` proved the directory is `vscode/`. Fixed in both the workflow and the changelog fragment.\n   - **secretlint \"config is not found\"** — needed `.secretlintrc.json`; copied the js template's.\n   - **secretlint `\"**/*\"` never finished** — still running after ~25 minutes locally (walks `target/`, `node_modules/`, ~150 MB of committed case-study logs). Killed it. Root cause: the glob scans the working tree, not the index. Fixed by rewriting to scan only the changed files; measured 2.6s on the PR diff. Recorded the measurement as the justification in both the script header and the workflow comment.\n   - **secretlint true-positive verification** — a fake AWS key was NOT flagged, so I re-tested with a `ghp_…` GitHub token, which was flagged (`[GITHUB_TOKEN] found GitHub Token`, exit 123). This confirms the gate actually fires.\n   - **Two wrong claims of my own, corrected before/while filing upstream**: (a) I had written that all three templates use `always() && !cancelled()`; measurement showed rust 7, js 0, python 6 — the js template already complies and is the reference implementation, so CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md §10 is right and rust/python are the outliers. (b) I had attributed the electron-builder warning to the custom `mac.sign` hook; reading `out/mac/MacTargetHelper.js:36-41` showed it fires on `qualifier === \"-\" && hardenedRuntime` alone and never reads `config.entitlements`.\n   - **`.github/dependabot.yml` gap claim is unsourced** — verified that none of the three templates ships one, so that row in analysis §7 should be corrected rather than acted on.\n   - **`sleep`-based waiting was blocked by the harness**; switched to `until … do sleep …; done` loops and `run_in_background`.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n\n   Closed in this session: R2 items 5 and 6 (desktop + `.vsix` packaging now gate PRs in dry-run mode) and R2 item 1 (Docker image build + the previously-callerless `verify-docker-runtime.sh` now gate PRs); the `always() && !cancelled()` best-practice violation (R5); R4 in full (four upstream issues filed with reproducible examples, workarounds and code suggestions, as the brief demands). In progress and uncommitted: R3/R5 adoption of `simulate-fresh-merge.sh`, a secrets scan, and the `setup-buildx-resilient` composite.\n\n   Still unexplained (deliberately instrumented, not guessed): why the custom macOS sign hook produced no output at all in CI. The unconditional `[adhoc-sign-mac] hook entered (debug=…)` banner added in the first commit exists precisely to answer that on the next run.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The task brief (carried over from the prior session): \"Download all logs and collect data related about the issue to this repository, and compile that data into the ./dev/log/issues/808/pulls/809 folder. Use the collected evidence to do a deep analysis (search online for additional facts and data), reconstruct the timeline/sequence of events, list each and every requirement from the issue, find the root cause of each problem, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement. Also check online for known existing components/libraries that solve a similar problem or can help. If there is not enough data to find the actual root cause, add debug output and a verbose mode (if not already present) so the root cause can be found on the next iteration. Keep the default state switched off. If the issue is related to another repository/project, report issues on GitHub for that project when possible. Each report must contain reproducible examples, workarounds, and suggestions for fixing the issue in code. Double-check that the requirements are fully applied to the entire codebase: if an issue exists in multiple places, apply it in all of them. Proceed.\"\n   - A continuation instruction to resume the last task without recapping.\n   - A final instruction to produce this summary as text only, with no tool calls.\n\n   No corrective feedback and no additional security constraints were given in this session. Standing constraints from the environment brief: push only to `issue-808-bf5af32dbcdd`; update PR 809 rather than creating a new one; preserve commit history.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **Commit and push the uncommitted R3/R5 work**: `scripts/simulate-fresh-merge.sh`, `scripts/check-secrets.sh`, `.secretlintrc.json`, `.secretlintignore` (keep or delete), `.github/actions/setup-buildx-resilient/action.yml`, and the `release.yml` changes (fresh-merge steps in `lint`/`test`, the `secrets-scan` job, the three buildx rewires). Must include a changelog-fragment update, an analysis.md §7/§10 update, and the `Formal-AI-Session`/`Formal-AI-Evidence` trailers, then re-verify with `rust-script scripts/self-hosting-metric.rs --since main --until HEAD`.\n   - Correct analysis §7: drop/annotate the `.github/dependabot.yml` row (no template ships one) and mark the now-closed rows (fresh-merge, secrets scan, buildx composite, `!cancelled()`).\n   - Remaining R2 backlog items (from analysis §6): `deploy-pages` artifact assembly / `test-e2e-pages`; crates.io publish path; `scripts/desktop-release-resolve.sh` logic; version-bump machinery.\n   - Remaining R3/R5 gaps: dedicated fast `cargo-lock` and file-size jobs, doc/link validation (lychee).\n   - Finalize: `gh pr edit` title/description for PR #809, merge `main` into the branch, verify CI green (download logs with `gh run view <id> --repo link-assistant/formal-ai --log` if not), check for new issue/PR comments, `gh pr ready 809`.\n\n8. Current Work:\n\n   I was mid-way through adopting the template best practices into our own repo (R3/R5) — none of it committed yet. The last action was fixing the `BASE_REF` expression in the new `secrets-scan` job (a `sed` had failed on the `||` characters, so I used Edit instead):\n\n   ```yaml\n           - name: Check for secrets\n             env:\n               # pull_request -> base branch; push -> the pre-push SHA;\n               # workflow_dispatch has neither, so scan the tip commit.\n               BASE_REF: ${{ github.base_ref || github.event.before || 'HEAD~1' }}\n             run: bash scripts/check-secrets.sh\n   ```\n\n   The Edit tool warned: \"the file had been modified on disk since you last read it — the edit applied cleanly, but the file contains other changes not in your context\", so `.github/workflows/release.yml` should be re-read before further context-dependent edits. YAML validity was last confirmed after the buildx rewire (`yaml ok`, job list `detect-changes,changelog,evidence-check,docker-build,secrets-scan,version-check,lint,test,coverage,build,auto-release,manual-release,changelog-pr,test-e2e-local,test-agent-cli-e2e,deploy-pages,test-e2e-pages`) but NOT after this final `BASE_REF` edit.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n\n   Re-read `.github/workflows/release.yml`, re-validate it with the `js-yaml` one-liner, then commit and push the pending R3/R5 batch (fresh-merge simulation, secrets scan, buildx-resilient composite) with the Formal-AI trailers, updating `changelog.d/20260720_140000_issue_808_ci_cd_fixes.md` and `analysis.md` §7/§10 in the same commit — including the §7 correction that no template ships `.github/dependabot.yml`. This continues the R3 line of work I stated when adopting the composite and the scripts, and matches the brief's \"Double-check that the requirements are fully applied to the entire codebase: if an issue exists in multiple places, apply it in all of them.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/box/.claude/projects/-tmp-gh-issue-solver-1784535043401/a7583710-f266-4c39-b5cf-8583e137ffd4.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."
