[2026-07-20T09:24:56.196Z] [INFO]           "command": "cat > /tmp/prbody.md <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n\nFixes the CI/CD defects behind issue #808 and moves the checks that previously\nonly ran on `main` into the pull-request stage, so a pull request can no longer\nbe green while the release it produces is broken.\n\nFixes #808\n\n## Root causes found (evidence in `dev/log/issues/808/pulls/809/`)\n\n1. **macOS codesign failure on release** — `codesign` refused the bundled Chrome\n   for Testing runtime (\"unsealed contents present in the root directory of an\n   embedded framework\"): its framework layout is not versioned. Fixed with\n   `mac.signIgnore`, independently of the custom sign hook.\n2. **The macOS sign hook produced no output at all** — this was unexplained, so\n   the first commit added an unconditional hook-entry banner and routed the\n   diagnostics to stderr. On the first pull-request packaging run that\n   instrumentation answered it: `app-builder-lib`'s `isSignAllowed()` returns\n   early with *\"Current build is a part of pull request, code signing will be\n   skipped\"* whenever `GITHUB_BASE_REF` is set, so the hook is never invoked and\n   the app ships without a `CodeResources` envelope. Fixed with\n   `CSC_FOR_PULL_REQUEST` on the ad-hoc step only (no secrets are in play there).\n3. **Auto Release blocked by a malformed self-hosting evidence trailer** — now\n   validated at pull-request time by a new `evidence-check` job.\n\n## All checks now run at the pull-request stage (issue comment 5020083365)\n\n- Desktop + `.vsix` packaging: the full six-target matrix, macOS signing and the\n  artifact smoke tests run on pull requests in **dry-run** mode — every\n  publishing step (attest, release upload, `SHA256SUMS`, `finalize`) is skipped.\n  Path-filtered so unrelated pull requests do not pay for six runners.\n- Docker image build + `verify-formal-ai-dind` runtime contract (`push: false`,\n  so it is fork-safe).\n- Self-hosting evidence trailers.\n- Secrets scan.\n- Fresh-merge simulation against the current `main`.\n\n## Practices adopted from the pipeline templates (R3/R5)\n\nCompared against `link-foundation/{rust,js,python}-ai-driven-development-pipeline-template`\nand `hive-mind/docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md`:\n\n- `scripts/simulate-fresh-merge.sh` (verbatim from the js template) — a stale\n  merge preview now fails the pull request instead of breaking `main`.\n- `scripts/check-secrets.sh` + `.secretlintrc.json`. Scoped to the files a change\n  touches: the template's `secretlint \"**/*\"` did not finish in 25 minutes on\n  this tree, while the diff scan measures 2.6 s. Verified it actually fires — a\n  planted `ghp_…` token is reported as `[GITHUB_TOKEN] found GitHub Token`.\n- `.github/actions/setup-buildx-resilient` (verbatim from the rust template),\n  replacing all three raw `docker/setup-buildx-action@v4` uses.\n- Replaced all nine `always() && !cancelled()` guards with `!cancelled()`\n  (best-practices §10): `always()` also runs the job when the run is *cancelled*,\n  which is the opposite of the intent.\n\n## Defects reported upstream (R4)\n\nFour issues filed with reproducible examples, workarounds and code suggestions —\nsee §8 of the analysis for the table and for two self-corrections I made while\nverifying my own earlier claims.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo test --test unit ci_cd::` — 131 passed. The workflow-invariant tests\n  were updated for the new jobs rather than around them.\n- `bash scripts/check-secrets.sh`, `bash scripts/simulate-fresh-merge.sh` and\n  `rust-script scripts/self-hosting-metric.rs --since main --until HEAD` all run\n  clean locally.\n- Regression test asserting the `mac.signIgnore` patterns match the browser\n  runtime and not the app binary.\nEOF\ngh pr edit 809 --repo link-assistant/formal-ai --title \"Fix CI/CD false positives and errors, and run every release check at the pull-request stage\" --body-file /tmp/prbody.md && echo ok"
