[2026-07-20T09:25:27.385Z] [INFO]         "text": "I'll wait for these runs to finish before doing anything further. Status so far:\n\n**Pushed since resuming** (branch `issue-808-bf5af32dbcdd`, PR [#809](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/809)):\n\n1. **R3/R5 adoption** — `scripts/simulate-fresh-merge.sh`, `scripts/check-secrets.sh` + `.secretlintrc.json` behind a new `secrets-scan` job, and `.github/actions/setup-buildx-resilient` replacing all three raw `docker/setup-buildx-action@v4` uses.\n2. **Merged the 14 new `main` commits** (only conflict was `.gitkeep` timestamps) and rewrote the two new commit messages to the session id the evidence file records — `self-hosting-metric.rs --since main --until HEAD` now reports 18.86% (7/20 commits) instead of erroring.\n3. **A real root cause the added instrumentation exposed.** The pull-request packaging dry run failed with *\"Mounted app is missing its signed CodeResources envelope\"* and the hook banner never printed. The packaging log shows `app-builder-lib`'s `isSignAllowed()` bailing with *\"Current build is a part of pull request, code signing will be skipped\"* — `builder-util`'s `isPullRequest()` is true whenever `GITHUB_BASE_REF` is set, so the custom `mac.sign` hook is never invoked. Fixed with `CSC_FOR_PULL_REQUEST: \"true\"` on the ad-hoc step only, where no signing secrets exist and the identity is `-`, so the flag's documented secret-leak concern does not apply.\n4. **Workflow-invariant tests updated for the new jobs** (`evidence-check`, `docker-build`, `secrets-scan`), and the `always() && !cancelled()` assertion replaced along with the stale comments; `cargo test --test unit ci_cd::` is 131/131 green locally.\n5. Analysis §7/§10 updated — including the correction that no template ships `.github/dependabot.yml`, so that row was never a real gap — plus changelog fragments and a rewritten PR title/description.\n\nThe PR is still a draft; I'll mark it ready once the runs on `ed943da` come back green (or investigate the logs if they don't)."
